From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: do not double count the tc-ets tx packets

airoha_qdma_get_tx_ets_stats() treats the two QDMA channel counters
(REG_CNTR_VAL(channel << 1) and REG_CNTR_VAL((channel << 1) + 1)) as two
independent sources and hands their summed delta to the qdisc bstats, so
`tc class show` reports about twice the packets the port transmitted.

They are not independent sources.  The second slot counts every packet
the channel transmitted; the first counts the subset of those the CPU
submitted (fwd >= cpu).  The measured delta(cpu+fwd)/delta(gdm1) of 2.08
on the XR1710G is exactly that double count (perf-roadmap Q22, M1.13b):
hardware forwarding is delta(fwd) - delta(cpu) and the offload ratio is
that share over delta(fwd), so fwd/(cpu+fwd) ratios are not meaningful.

Report delta(fwd) alone as the channel's tx_packets.  cpu_tx_packets and
fwd_tx_packets stay separate and both are still advanced on every query,
so the next delta of either slot starts from the same instant; only the
value handed to the qdisc changes.

This is an accounting fix, not a performance change: forwarding is
untouched, and so are dev->stats.tx_ok_pkts and the port MIBs.  No
throughput conclusion is drawn from this patch.

Board check: over the same window, `tc class show` tx packets divided by
the port MIB tx packets must be 1 +/- 0.01.

Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3157,12 +3157,20 @@ static int airoha_qdma_get_tx_ets_stats(
 	cpu_tx_packets = airoha_qdma_rr(qdma, REG_CNTR_VAL(channel << 1));
 	fwd_tx_packets = airoha_qdma_rr(qdma,
 					REG_CNTR_VAL((channel << 1) + 1));
-	tx_packets = (u32)(cpu_tx_packets -
-			   dev->qos_stats[channel].cpu_tx_packets);
-	tx_packets += (u32)(fwd_tx_packets -
-			    dev->qos_stats[channel].fwd_tx_packets);
+	/* fwd counts every packet the channel transmitted and cpu the
+	 * subset of them the CPU submitted (fwd >= cpu): the two slots are
+	 * stages of the same channel, not independent sources.  Adding both
+	 * deltas counted the CPU-submitted packets twice and inflated the
+	 * qdisc stats by about cpu/fwd.  Report the channel total only.
+	 */
+	tx_packets = (u32)(fwd_tx_packets -
+			   dev->qos_stats[channel].fwd_tx_packets);
 
 	_bstats_update(opt->stats.bstats, 0, tx_packets);
+
+	/* Both baselines advance together so the next query takes its two
+	 * deltas over the same window.
+	 */
 	dev->qos_stats[channel].cpu_tx_packets = cpu_tx_packets;
 	dev->qos_stats[channel].fwd_tx_packets = fwd_tx_packets;
 
